    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="1209" n="1195" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1195"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.00/5–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-12T15:00:00-04:00">May 12, 1948—3 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. Reur 342, May 11,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d798-f1"/> Secy made following
                    statement press conference noon May 12: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Korean people are to be congratulated on the success of Korea’s
                            first democratic election on Monday, held under the observation of the
                            United Nations Temporary Commission on Korea. The fact that some 90
                            percent of the registered voters cast their ballots, despite the lawless
                            efforts of a Communist-dominated minority to prevent or sabotage the
                            election, is a clear revelation that the Korean people are determined to
                            form their own government by democratic means”.<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d798-f2"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d798-f1" n="1" xml:id="d798-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d798-f2" n="2" xml:id="d798-f2-content">
                <p>Dr. Syngman Rhee sent a telegram of thanks through B. C. Limb, Chairman of the
                    Korean Commission, Washington, on May 17.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
